# Build-context filter for Dockerfile.test. BuildKit prefers a
# <dockerfile>.dockerignore over the top-level .dockerignore, so this file
# is what applies when building the test image. Unlike the prod
# .dockerignore, it KEEPS tests/ and app/ (the suite needs them) and only
# drops the genuinely irrelevant/heavy paths.
.git
.venv
.env
.claude
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
docs/
scratch/
dist/
*.md
!README.md
